text:
After almost 6 years of beta testing since this game's "release" I was expecting Cyberbug 2077 to be at least decent, and I turned out to be wrong

Within 92 hours of playing this, there hasn't been a single (yes, NOT ONE) game session in which I did not encounter a bug. Granted, the sessions weren't exactly short ones (4-5 hours on average), but I still find it unacceptable. Those bugs aren't gamebreaking (except one), but are annoying and noticeable. The bugs I have encountered include but are not limited to:
-Not being able to loot the box/chest/whatever to get an item that is needed to finish an NCPD assault (game's most basic side-quests). Required game restart to fix, happened about 5 times total;
-Enemies seeing me through walls, enemies seeing other incapacitated enemies through walls (I was mainly doing a stealth playthrough);
-Game having a chance to flashbang me any time I close the map. Might be related to me playing with HDR on, but I did not research it;
-Cars' inner lights turning on automatically and refusing to turn off (I drive mainly in first person and that shit is really annoying);
-Stamina bar not showing up when it's supposed to;
-Stamina bar showing up when it's not supposed to;
-NPCs holding invisible weapons;
-Doubling NPCs. One time I had 2 different shopkeepers standing in exact same place, other time I had double dialogue choices for the same shopkeeper;
-NPCs in the cars going haywire for no reason and start crashing into everything;
-NPCs in the cars repeatedly slamming into exact same wall;
-NPCs in the cars just standing there doing nothing when path is clear for them to drive;
-Cars that just fly up in the air on the spot;
-Cars that get stuck in the ground;
-NPCs on the sidewalks actively trying to jump under my wheels;
-Inconsistencies with enemies reacting to sounds;
-Enemies that get stuck in the ground;
-Enemies in any vehicle that just don't react to anything unless you walk in front of them and enter combat;
-Picking up an un

Se você é um cara que gosta de usar HACK e se divertir, podem baixar o jogo.
Agora se você é um cara que gosta de jogar limpo, ser honesto, gente boa, que tem sua PAZ (NÃO BAIXE ESSE JOGO) pois os desenvolvedores só querem seu dinheiro e não estão nem aí para você, isso é comprovado por não terem um suporte que realmente ajuda. 
@VALVE, QUER DINHEIRO, DINHEIRO E DINHEIRO.

/*

one of the best computer games ever made. do you like dungeons & dragons? real time travel with turn-based combat? a rich and epic fantasy role-playing game? then this is for you. a most worthy successor to the classic baldur's gate 1 & 2, which adds to every possible facet of the game series. a awesome and sprawling piece of playable art. story, characters, voice acting, graphics, music, quests, items, maps... everything is top-notch. the ability to play solo, local split-screen co-op or multiplayer co-op just adds to the depth of this legendary game. this is a story every gamer needs to play.

*/

